<article>
	<h1><span>Mass Mail: Mailings</span></h1>

	<ul class="nav">
		<li><a href="#overview">Overview</a></li>
		<li><a href="#column-headers">Column Headers</a></li>
		<li><a href="#list-filters">List Filters</a></li>
		<li><a href="#toolbar">Toolbar</a></li>
		<li><a href="#sub-menu">Sub-menu Links</a></li>
	</ul>

	<section id="overview">
		<h2><span>Overview</span></h2>

		<p>This screen lists mass mailings, most recently created first. Click a mailing's ID, subject or status to
			open it. When there are no mailings, the list shows <em>No mailings yet.</em></p>
	</section>
	<section id="column-headers">
		<h2><span>Column Headers</span></h2>

		<dl>
			<dt>Checkbox</dt>
			<dd>Check this box to select one or more items. To select all items, check the box in the column heading.
				After one or more boxes are checked, click a toolbar button to take an action on the selected item or
				items.</dd>

			<dt>ID</dt>
			<dd>This is a unique identification number for this item assigned automatically by the system.</dd>

			<dt>Subject</dt>
			<dd>The mailing's subject. A <strong>!</strong> badge, titled <em>Ignores opt-out</em>, marks a mailing
				that ignores users' opt-out preferences.</dd>

			<dt>Status</dt>
			<dd>The mailing's status: Draft, Pending approval, Held, Scheduled, Preparing, Sending, Paused, Sent or
				Cancelled.</dd>

			<dt>Sent / Total</dt>
			<dd>The number of messages sent and the total number of recipients. When any failed, the number of
				failures follows in parentheses.</dd>

			<dt>Created by</dt>
			<dd>The name of the user who created the mailing.</dd>

			<dt>Created</dt>
			<dd>The date the mailing was created.</dd>
		</dl>
	</section>
	<section id="list-filters">
		<h2><span>List Filters</span></h2>

		<dl>
			<dt>Search</dt>
			<dd>Lists only mailings whose subject contains the text. The <strong>Search</strong> button applies it and
				the <strong>Clear</strong> button empties the filters.</dd>

			<dt>Status</dt>
			<dd>Lists only mailings with the chosen status. <strong>- All statuses -</strong> lists every
				mailing.</dd>
		</dl>
	</section>
	<section id="toolbar">
		<h2><span>Toolbar</span></h2>
		<p>At the top right you will see the toolbar.</p>
		<p>The functions are:</p>
		<dl>
			<dt>Options</dt>
			<dd>Opens the Options window where settings such as default parameters or permissions can be edited.
				Shown only to users who may configure the component.</dd>

			<dt>Delete</dt>
			<dd>Shown only to users who may delete. After asking for confirmation, permanently deletes the selected
				mailings with their recipient records and attachments. Only a mailing that has not started sending
				and is a Draft, Held, Pending approval, Scheduled or Cancelled can be deleted. Other selected mailings
				are kept, and a message says how many.</dd>

			<dt>New</dt>
			<dd>Shown only to users who may create. Opens the screen to compose a new mailing.</dd>

			<dt>Help</dt>
			<dd>Opens this help screen.</dd>
		</dl>
	</section>
	<section id="sub-menu">
		<h2><span>Sub-menu Links</span></h2>
		<p>At the top left, you will see sub-menu options. The links are:</p>
		<dl>
			<dt>Status Dashboard</dt>
			<dt>Mailings (this page)</dt>
		</dl>
		<p>At the right of the sub-menu, a status indicator shows whether mail can go out. Point at it for
			details.</p>
		<dl>
			<dt>Sending disabled</dt>
			<dd>Sending is turned off in the options. New mailings are held and nothing is delivered.</dd>

			<dt>Cron stopped</dt>
			<dd>Sending is on, but the delivery cron job is not running. Mail is queued and does not go out.</dd>

			<dt>Mail system OK</dt>
			<dd>Sending is on and the delivery cron job is running.</dd>
		</dl>
	</section>
</article>
